    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0736" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2265f: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Barcelona</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Franklin</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-23T19:00:00-04:00">July 23, 1936—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Belgian Government has requested our cooperation in the evacuation of Belgian
                    nationals from Barcelona. The Commanding Officer of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Exeter</hi> has been informed of this and we have also informed <pb
                        facs="0737" n="638" xml:id="pg638"/> the Belgian Government that while space
                    on the vessel is limited, we will give every consideration to its request.</p>
                <p>We assume that such Americans as avail themselves of the use of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Exeter</hi> will be sufficiently supplied with funds so
                    as to take care of themselves. We very much hope that this is the situation
                    since we have no particular funds available for this purpose. However, you
                    should let us know whether there are any destitute Americans in need of
                    funds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
